                        ],
                        "form": "huwelijkssluitingen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4bed2fc-4eb6-381c-9c54-d2ab90413b38",
                        "entry_id": "d4bb7aa5-3ca8-3d7b-97f0-e88487701432",
                        "glosses": [
                            "de ceremonie waarin men met elkaar trouwt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28b843e9-53a9-40cd-94d9-459c63c25bb0",
                                "sense_id": "c4bed2fc-4eb6-381c-9c54-d2ab90413b38",
                                "text": "Steeds minder Italianen halen een boterbriefje. Het aantal huwelijkssluitingen is in zes jaar tijd met een kwart geslonken van ruim 246.000 in 2008 tot ruim 189.000 in 2014. Het daalt daarmee sneller dan in andere Europese landen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39e4776f-e39b-478d-b22d-0c97ec01c903",
                                "sense_id": "c4bed2fc-4eb6-381c-9c54-d2ab90413b38",
                                "text": "Zo is het aantal huwelijkssluitingen tussen twee mannen in 2011 gedaald naar 601, terwijl dat het jaar ervoor nog 660 waren. Het aantal huwelijken tussen twee vrouwen is juist gestegen, van 694 in 2010 tot 754 in 2011. Sowieso blijken lesbiennes trouwlustiger dan homo's: hun aandeel in het totale aantal trouwpartijen is ieder jaar hoger dan dat van hun mannelijke evenknieën."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df1f60fa-8b44-45e4-b341-318f1152ac08",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4bb7aa5-3ca8-3d7b-97f0-e88487701432",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4bed2fc-4eb6-381c-9c54-d2ab90413b38",
                        "target_lang_word": "wedding",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wedding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3c6b94c-f893-3934-8c0e-be683a7b5724",
                                        "entry_id": "6acc704e-e1bc-331a-ac4d-8d4299736f66",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of wed"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "899a570d-3230-45c8-9267-e20a60dcdd31",
                                                "sense_id": "f3c6b94c-f893-3934-8c0e-be683a7b5724",
                                                "text": "Accordingly the Prince, accepting her largesse, sought the King to whom he had pledged his parents (and they were still with him in all weal and welfare) and going in to him made his salam and kissed ground and told him the whole tale of the past and the conditions of death or marriage he had made with the King's daughter and of his wedding her after overcoming her in contention."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wedding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "137c170c-0b43-3cdf-807b-fc02f9d0f601",
                                        "entry_id": "bb29cb06-d1cb-3b98-85d3-db9753215693",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A marriage ceremony; a ritual officially celebrating the beginning of a marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "173dfe3a-fb04-4652-8112-631c1a29526b",
                                                "sense_id": "137c170c-0b43-3cdf-807b-fc02f9d0f601",
                                                "text": "Her announcement was quite a surprise, coming a month after she published the words \"I hate weddings with a passion and a fury I can only partially explain rationally.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6664c89-04ff-450e-80c3-61fe2e2e3c10",
                                                "sense_id": "137c170c-0b43-3cdf-807b-fc02f9d0f601",
                                                "text": "Simple and brief was the wedding, as that of Ruth and of Boaz."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac422e83-3490-40ca-901d-0d1dcfe601c5",
                                                "sense_id": "137c170c-0b43-3cdf-807b-fc02f9d0f601",
                                                "text": "Rumor has it that there will be a wedding in our village ere the daisies are in bloom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "738e672d-864d-41ba-bcdd-4cb43b58766d",
                                                "sense_id": "137c170c-0b43-3cdf-807b-fc02f9d0f601",
                                                "text": "After the wedding there was singing and concertina-playing in the laundry till late evening."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                        "entry_id": "bb29cb06-d1cb-3b98-85d3-db9753215693",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The joining of two or more parts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc6249d3-c714-489b-89ff-d640f4be603e",
                                                "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                                "text": "The wedding of our three companies took place last week."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37a4b556-2c09-400f-b8a8-a9a5491352f6",
                                                "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                                "text": "1900, Eve Emery Dye, McLoughlin and Old Oregon, 2005 facsimile edition, page 56,\nThat wedding of the fur companies is historic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba614894-63d3-4e7f-892c-60c04e8062ce",
                                                "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                                "text": "Significantly, Grand Metropolitan elaborates upon the wedding of tradition and consumer narcissim that is the distinctively British version of private-sector collective representations;[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad578447-548e-403a-ac86-bb9ca2b81dff",
                                                "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                                "text": "The wedding of commercial with universal banking would result in more careful project evaluation and selection and a closer monitoring of existing loans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "901d4814-a002-4cd0-921b-4cdec854a66c",
                                                "sense_id": "d9355cc5-3c27-3370-8bb1-92240b33d88c",
                                                "text": "The wedding of black brass bands and orchestras to jubilee concert companies was a consolidation that favored both promoters and musicians."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wedding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                        "entry_id": "1920b745-c301-382f-809d-9271b794d35e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To participate in a wedding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "humorous",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95935094-fd04-4dee-bb6f-9b1ebd61001d",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "\"Snowball\" was the name of this good steed, and great care had evidently been taken in her grooming to make her worthy of her name, her bridle being also gaily decked with coloured ribbons, for, as John said, when attending to these duties, \"You don't go out a weddinging every day, do you, old gal?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5ff3ed-7c19-41ea-892c-866e58d85eec",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "\"Where you goin' get weddinged?\" she inquired one day. / \"We shall be married at the Episcopal Church, Yin Yang,\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f84ca79d-8068-4edd-9204-0d63f84ce168",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "Getting married is entirely different than getting weddinged."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a153b901-6eaf-49fb-99bb-9e79d5063f85",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "(In her private life this year, three of her children have been married, in quick succession, leaving her \"weddinged out.\")"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f351524d-cd56-48dd-a7cf-d079b805504a",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "It was the most opportune time; I had my agenda and she had hers, and I suspected that she and Susan would be “weddinged” out by the time they got home"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21a70f2e-c261-4698-9244-c7a8589a04e1",
                                                "sense_id": "65b81b00-6f39-35ec-b5e6-25b48f3bc161",
                                                "text": "Wasn't he the dude she weddinged with in her \"Love All Over Me\" vid? Sure was. . ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5534a726-0897-42e7-be28-3be43df48a5e",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4bb7aa5-3ca8-3d7b-97f0-e88487701432",
                        "source_sense_id": "c4bed2fc-4eb6-381c-9c54-d2ab90413b38",
                        "target_lang_word": "marriage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "marriage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "318a783c-a6dc-35ef-8fd0-21c0864d3e1f",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being married."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6aca277f-89ff-4770-a90c-dc1b913c407d",
                                                "sense_id": "318a783c-a6dc-35ef-8fd0-21c0864d3e1f",
                                                "text": "You should enter marriage for love."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A union of two or more people that creates a family tie and carries legal, social, and/or religious rights and responsibilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9961d939-a55a-4ca2-9eec-fab909bca721",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                                "text": "By his marriage to his two wives, Tapuwae quietly strengthened all of the pas of the Wairoa district, as many of them came under his control through these unions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4640bbaa-5286-44bd-ac21-3816a6aef8f6",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                                "text": "One layman in Buddha's time decided to embrace celibacy and relinquished his marriage vows to his four wives. When he asked them what they wanted in terms of a settlement, one said, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20aca7d7-5a73-4549-a7a9-e808808151a9",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                                "text": "The account of the loss of the blessing of his father Isaac appears immediately after Esau's marriage to his Hittite wives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "990a9bde-371b-4aea-93fc-ec0cd311bf5c",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                                "text": "In an open marriage, the partners are free to have extramarital relationships or sex without betraying one another. Such a marriage is based on communication, trust, and respect, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "701bf829-2a30-41b8-902c-ef087bdb538c",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1bb41b-8888-3333-a4e5-b34fb43ed3ba",
                                                "text": "Now can we eat? Marriages are arranged for whatever purpose is suitable. All this talk of undying love and childbearing squirms in my stomach like a worm that demands feeding."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2313691-03ce-347c-ac90-95fe6e6356ff",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A union of two or more people that creates a family tie and carries legal, social, and/or religious rights and responsibilities.",
                                            "The union of only two people, to the exclusion of all others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "specifically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2b0d23d-3a64-410a-a2d3-b50c74c4ab7b",
                                                "sense_id": "c2313691-03ce-347c-ac90-95fe6e6356ff",
                                                "text": "Pat and Leslie's marriage to each other lasted forty years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fa9df56-c67e-4b3a-a477-bd64c24b8cfd",
                                                "sense_id": "c2313691-03ce-347c-ac90-95fe6e6356ff",
                                                "text": "\"I have a patient right now whose marriage proved to be a tragedy. She wanted love, sexual gratification, children, and social prestige; but life blasted all her hopes. Her husband didn't love her. He refused even to eat with her, and forced her to serve his meals in his room upstairs. She had no children, no social standing. She went insane; and, in her imagination, she divorced her husband and resumed her maiden name. She now believes she has married into the English aristocracy, and she insists on being called Lady Smith."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0f8a274-3de0-4863-ad6f-a56521c65bc6",
                                                "sense_id": "c2313691-03ce-347c-ac90-95fe6e6356ff",
                                                "text": "My grandparents' marriage lasted for forty years."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c357b0ab-756d-34e5-b554-6c7d2857aaa5",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A union of two or more people that creates a family tie and carries legal, social, and/or religious rights and responsibilities.",
                                            "The union of two people of opposite sex, to the exclusion of all others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "often",
                                            "specifically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8533896d-b832-374c-baf3-01ef4b9375f1",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wedding; a ceremony in which people wed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddba87c3-8957-4485-b973-451c32e6027a",
                                                "sense_id": "8533896d-b832-374c-baf3-01ef4b9375f1",
                                                "text": "You are cordially invited to the marriage of James Smith and Jane Doe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36f2447e-845e-3ab4-81f4-585eb0b64dd7",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A close union."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61780c11-2a22-43d8-8347-5a6ceeadf96d",
                                                "sense_id": "36f2447e-845e-3ab4-81f4-585eb0b64dd7",
                                                "text": "And this marriage of poetry and history remained a solid relationship throughout the classical period."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80871c3a-09e1-48fd-9624-a6579b17d5e4",
                                                "sense_id": "36f2447e-845e-3ab4-81f4-585eb0b64dd7",
                                                "text": "Above all, we will no longer have to feel qualms about the marriage of art and money. We will no longer have to wonder if it is possible to separate the esthetic value of an art work from its commercial value."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19ebc8cb-c27b-4bf7-8fad-2cbd45485b19",
                                                "sense_id": "36f2447e-845e-3ab4-81f4-585eb0b64dd7",
                                                "text": "But the food is real: a marriage of local ingredients and serious technique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa697f0c-5603-403f-9fd7-0406923f70f7",
                                                "sense_id": "36f2447e-845e-3ab4-81f4-585eb0b64dd7",
                                                "text": "That bitter rivalry -- between Thaksin's supporters, known as the Red Shirts, and the royalist elites, known as the Yellow Shirts -- has been a hallmark of politics for the past 20 years, with deadly street protests a common occurrence. Friday's announcement signals a surprise marriage between the two sides, with Ubolratana having the power to break that cycle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a85e052c-6d65-333e-85ef-380bfb434bb6",
                                        "entry_id": "5e5f833e-4d97-365e-b46c-43fa738308b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A joining of two parts."
                                        ],
